% Bibliography for the papers this codebase is built against.
%
% The PDFs themselves are NOT in this repository and must not be (see
% MANIFEST.md); this file is metadata only, which carries no such restriction.
%
% Provenance: every entry in the curated sections below was rebuilt on
% 2026-08-29 from the document's own front matter and from its DOI record
% (Crossref / DataCite content negotiation), not from memory. Volume, issue,
% page range, article number and DOI have each been checked against at least one
% of those two sources; where the two disagreed, the DOI record won and the
% disagreement is recorded in the entry's `note`. Every such entry has a PDF in
% literature/, and `scripts/check_literature.py` enforces that.
%
% The final section, "Extended set", was added on 2026-08-29 in a lighter pass:
% bibliographic records only, from each document's DOI record (and, for ACM
% article numbers, the PDF's own reference block). No abstracts were extracted
% for these, so they have no block in ABSTRACTS.md and no editorial `note`; the
% DOI-wins rule still applies, and early-view-vs-volume-year discrepancies are
% noted. Three arrivals had no usable text layer (scanned Gingold & Monaghan
% 1977, Monaghan 1992, Monaghan 1994); their PDFs are parked in
% literature/scans/ and are deliberately absent from this file.
%
% Citation keys are `firstauthor + year`, suffixed when that collides, and the
% PDF filenames in this directory are `<key>_<slug>.pdf`. The shorthands used
% by DFSPH_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md 5 map as: [C] = cornelis2019, [BK] = bender2015,
% [I] = ihmsen2014, [B] = band2018, [BWJ23] = bender2023.


